          "page": 3,
          "section": "3.1 Microstructure of initial BG sample",
          "quote": "The volume fraction of the carbides is 5.7%, as shown in Fig. 1b. BSE images in Fig. 1c, d display the size and distribution of the carbides. A further examination in Fig. 1d reveals that the remarkable pinning of carbides is observed in the FG regions. The carbides are on the sub-micrometer scale, * 200–500 nm. The majority of the carbides exists on the grain boundaries (GBs) and twin boundaries of the FGs, as well as the pre-existing slip bands formed during deformation [16]. However, carbides are nearly free in the interiors of the CGs.",
